Backport: vo_gpu: fill the padding of the scaler LUT
Origin: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/commit/72d43dc9c999a21d867cdc0f934f3e4cd2195aa9
Upstream-Date: 2026-09-29
Upstream-Issue: https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/pull/18540
Applied-to: mpv 0.38.0 after the existing four playback patches
Modified-by: ChengYingPlayer maintainers, 2026-10-09

This is the complete six-line upstream fix. Only hunk line numbers and trailing
context are adapted to the pinned release after the existing playback patches.
Rows of six weights occupy two RGBA texels. Fill the two unused components with
the same channels of the preceding texel, instead of uploading uninitialized
memory. This preserves all computed weights, kernel choices and public ABI.
The original upstream source notices and applicable license terms remain intact.

--- a/video/out/gpu/video.c
+++ b/video/out/gpu/video.c
@@ -1782,6 +1782,12 @@ static void reinit_scaler(struct gl_video *p, struct scaler *scaler,
     float *weights = talloc_array(NULL, float, lut_size * stride);
     mp_compute_lut(scaler->kernel, lut_size, stride, weights);
 
+    for (int n = 0; n < lut_size; n++) {
+        float *row = weights + n * stride;
+        for (int i = size; i < stride; i++)
+            row[i] = row[i - num_components];
+    }
+
     bool use_1d = scaler->kernel->polar && (p->ra->caps & RA_CAP_TEX_1D);
 
     struct ra_tex_params lut_params = {
